.Dd August 28, 2026
.Dt PMC.AMDIOMMU 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pmc.amdiommu
.Nd measurements using AMD IOMMU performance counters
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libpmc
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In pmc.h
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Pp
The
.Nm AMDIOMMU
class supports optional filter qualifiers to narrow counting:
.Bl -tag -width .Li domain=N
.It Li domain=N
Count only transactions from DMA domain
.Ar N .
.It Li pasid=N
Count only transactions with PASID
.Ar N
(20-bit maximum).
.It Li devid=N
Count only transactions from device ID
.Ar N .
.El
.Pp
Filters are specified as a comma-separated suffix:
.Li AMDIOMMU_MEM_TRANS_TOTAL,domain=5 .
.Tn AMD
IOMMU units that implement the optional Performance Counter Support
extension
.Pq EFR[PCSup]=1
expose a set of hardware event counters accessible via MMIO at offset
0x4000h in the IOMMU register space.
The
.Li PMC_CLASS_AMDIOMMU
class provides access to these counters.
.Pp
Each counter-capable IOMMU unit presents
.Em N
counter banks, each containing
.Em M
independent 48-bit up-counting registers.
The geometry is reported at initialisation time by reading the
Performance Counter Configuration register
.Pq MMIO 0x4000h .
All counters within a unit are system-wide
.Pq Li PMC_MODE_SC
and are not associated with any particular CPU.
.Pp
Counters do not overflow-interrupt; the
.Li PMC_CAP_INTERRUPT
capability is not advertised.
Counter values must be sampled periodically to avoid silent wrap.
.Pp
Events do not take qualifiers; the event specifier must consist of
exactly the event name with no trailing comma or keyword.
.Ss Event Specifiers
The following events are supported.
Event names use the prefix
.Li AMDIOMMU- .
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Li AMDIOMMU-MEM_PASS_UNTRANS
Memory transactions passed without translation
.Pq DeviceID bypass or exclusion range .
.It Li AMDIOMMU-MEM_PASS_PRETRANS
Memory transactions passed via pre-translation
.Pq IOMMU disabled for device, or HostAddress .
.It Li AMDIOMMU-MEM_PASS_EXCL
Memory transactions passed because the address fell in the exclusion
range.
.It Li AMDIOMMU-MEM_TARGET_ABORT
Memory transactions that resulted in a target abort.
.It Li AMDIOMMU-MEM_TRANS_TOTAL
Total memory transactions processed by the IOMMU.
.It Li AMDIOMMU-MEM_IOMMU_TLB_PTE_HIT
IOMMU TLB hits on PTE-level entries.
.It Li AMDIOMMU-MEM_IOMMU_TLB_PTE_MIS
IOMMU TLB misses requiring a PTE-level page walk.
.It Li AMDIOMMU-MEM_IOMMU_TLB_PDE_HIT
IOMMU TLB hits on PDE-level (large page) entries.
.It Li AMDIOMMU-MEM_IOMMU_TLB_PDE_MIS
IOMMU TLB misses requiring a PDE-level page walk.
.It Li AMDIOMMU-MEM_DTE_HIT
Device table entry
.Pq DTE
hits in the DTE cache.
.It Li AMDIOMMU-MEM_DTE_MIS
DTE cache misses requiring a memory fetch.
.It Li AMDIOMMU-PAGE_TBL_READ_TOT
Total page table reads
.Pq nested and non-nested combined .
.It Li AMDIOMMU-PAGE_TBL_READ_NST
Non-nested
.Pq host-only
page table reads.
.It Li AMDIOMMU-PAGE_TBL_READ_GST
Guest page table reads
.Pq nested translation, GVA to GPA .
.It Li AMDIOMMU-INT_DTE_HIT
Interrupt DTE cache hits.
.It Li AMDIOMMU-INT_DTE_MIS
Interrupt DTE cache misses.
.It Li AMDIOMMU-CMD_PROCESSED
Total commands processed from the command buffer.
.It Li AMDIOMMU-CMD_PROCESSED_INV
Invalidation commands processed
.Pq INVALIDATE_IOMMU_PAGES, INVALIDATE_IOTLB_PAGES, etc. .
.It Li AMDIOMMU-TLB_INV
TLB invalidation operations initiated by the IOMMU.
.It Li AMDIOMMU-IGN_RD_WR_MMIO_1FF8H
Ignored reads or writes to MMIO offset 0x1FF8h
.Pq reserved register accesses .
.It Li AMDIOMMU-VAPIC_INT_NON_GUEST
Virtual APIC interrupts delivered to a non-guest target.
.It Li AMDIOMMU-VAPIC_INT_GUEST
Virtual APIC interrupts delivered to a guest target.
.It Li AMDIOMMU-SMI_RECV
SMI interrupts received by the IOMMU.
.It Li AMDIOMMU-SMI_BLK
SMI interrupts blocked by the IOMMU.
.El
.Ss Counter Scope
IOMMU counters measure activity at the IOMMU unit level, not at
individual CPU level.
Each unit is independent; on multi-socket systems with one IOMMU per
socket, results must not be summed across units without accounting for
the device topology.
.Pp
The class advertises
.Li PMC_CAP_SYSWIDE
and
.Li PMC_CAP_DOMWIDE .
.Xr pmcstat 8
allocates one counter per NUMA domain.
To measure a specific unit, bind the PMC to a CPU that belongs to the
NUMA domain associated with that IOMMU.
.Ss Privilege
Allocating an AMD IOMMU PMC requires the
.Li PRIV_PMC_SYSTEM
privilege.
Unprivileged allocation requests fail with
.Er EPERM .
.Sh EXAMPLES
Count the total IOMMU memory transactions on the first NUMA domain
for one second:
.Dl pmcstat -s AMDIOMMU-MEM_TRANS_TOTAL sleep 1
.Pp
Simultaneously monitor TLB hit and miss rates across two NUMA domains
.Pq CPUs 0 and 64
on a two-socket system:
.Dl pmcstat -c 0 -s AMDIOMMU-MEM_IOMMU_TLB_PTE_HIT -c 64 -s AMDIOMMU-MEM_IOMMU_TLB_PTE_HIT sleep 1
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pmc 3 ,
.Xr pmc.rapl 3 ,
.Xr pmc_allocate 3 ,
.Xr pmc_read 3 ,
.Xr pmclog 3 ,
.Xr hwpmc 4 ,
.Xr pmcstat 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Li PMC_CLASS_AMDIOMMU
class first appeared in
.Fx 16.0 .
.Sh CAVEATS
Counter values are 48 bits wide and wrap silently.
The maximum measurable count before wrap at a sustained rate of
10\~billion transactions per second is approximately 32\~days.
Consumers must read counters at a period shorter than the wrap
interval for the expected event rate.
.Pp
The counter control register
.Pq Fxn=0x10
bank-lock registers
.Pq 0x4008, 0x4010, 0x4018
must not be held locked when programming event sources, as writes to
filter fields are silently ignored while a bank is locked.
The driver does not program filter fields in this release; this caveat
applies to future qualifier extensions.
